# Curated data for the dashboard (map/index.html). Imported by build.py.
#
# ROUTES      every card belongs to exactly one proof route. A new card in build.py needs its id in one "nodes" list.
#             state: active (worked on now) | stalled (no current idea) | open (the goal itself).
#             key: the cards to read first, in order. gap: what is missing, in one or two sentences.
# HIGHLIGHTS  what the front page shows: lead (promising, not proved), result (proved or complete search), dead (ruled out).
#             Order within a kind is the order shown. Dates come from card_dates.txt, not from here.
# FAMILIES    the encyclopedia of kinds of arrangement. test names a membership test in map/index.html (FAM_TESTS).
#             group "tree": parent means "is a special case of". group "other": families that cut across the tree.
#
# Every sentence here must be checkable against the card it points to. Say "tested" for what is tested,
# and say who checked a proof when no person has read it.

